New **display** column or cell string: add it in `monitor_views` first, then bind Qt and WEB. Do not compose Auto MTO / ` AB` / robot-origin / AN tooltip in `window.py` or JS. New feature on another tab still calls `get_*` / `list_*` for facts; the painted row comes from `monitor_views`. Issuance-journal writes go through `apply_journal_decision` (validates, then `upsert_issuance_review`). Do not copy regex from `kits.py` into the widget. Never write issuance decisions onto `issuance_send` or Google «Выдача РД ПД».

### Algorithm versions

- Overlay: `OVERLAY_ALGORITHM_VERSION`
- MTO compare: `MTO_COMPARE_ALGORITHM_VERSION`
- Presence matrix flags/summary: `KIT_MATRIX_ALGORITHM_VERSION` — **do not bump** for working/official split or the issuance journal.
- Pipeline status: `PIPELINE_STATUS_ALGORITHM_VERSION` in [`rd_catalog/pipeline.py`](rd_catalog/pipeline.py) is **10**. Store it on `kit_pipeline.algorithm_version`. v5 treats a manual working mark as one issued **folder**, not the whole filename revision. v6 does not treat a shared NN as working: `10_SQ-…` with `01-AN01` stays official when `10_рев.…_as built` is the working as-build. v7 auto-working is overlay-current (newest NN) strictly above last send/F, not the globally highest filename on disk (leftover `01` in an earlier folder must not beat current `0-AN01`). v8 persists `working_as_build` so Комплекты «Рабочая рев. РД» can paint ` AB` (startup rebuild fills it). v9 skips **annulled** folders (`kit_annulled_flag`) from official / auto-working / transfer contests / heatmap collision join (overlay `detected_current` stays objective). v10 re-derives F letters after Unicode dash normalize (`02–AN02` → `02-AN02`) so a stored `google_event` from the old parser does not keep a stale bare `02`.
- Per-revision MTO heatmap: `REVISION_MATRIX_ALGORITHM_VERSION` in `rd_catalog/pipeline.py` (start at `1`). Store it on `kit_revision_cell.algorithm_version`. **Do not bump** for working/official split or folder-annulled. New fill key `annulled` / letter `Ан` is written on the next pipeline rebuild (v9 hatch).

## 2. Schema version 12

`SCHEMA_VERSION` is **12**. Keep `_migrate_2_to_3` and `_migrate_3_to_4`. `_migrate_4_to_5` in `rd_catalog/db.py` is ALTER `kit_pipeline` only. `_migrate_5_to_6` adds `mto_pair_comparison`. `_migrate_6_to_7` creates `issuance_review`. `_migrate_7_to_8` creates `an_mto_file`. `_migrate_8_to_9` creates `kit_working_flag`. `_migrate_9_to_10` rekeys `kit_working_flag` to the issued **folder** (`transfer_name` UNIQUE, plus `sequence`) and adds `kit_pipeline.working_transfer_names_json` / `working_sequences_json`. `_migrate_10_to_11` creates `file_mtime_override`. `_migrate_11_to_12` creates `kit_annulled_flag` (same folder identity as working). Do not rebuild `file_entry`. Worklist / `FolderTreeHint` MTO fields are a read view over `kit_revision_cell` — **no extra schema bump**. User liquidity, issuance-journal decisions, manual working flags, **manual annulled flags**, and MTO catalog-date overrides live in SQLite and **must survive** `replace_google_snapshot`, `replace_kit_derived`, `rebuild_pipeline`, scan upserts, and revision-matrix rebuild (never `DELETE FROM kit_liquidity_review`, `issuance_review`, `kit_working_flag`, `kit_annulled_flag`, or `file_mtime_override` during rebuild). `an_mto_file` must survive those same rebuilds (never `DELETE FROM an_mto_file` during them). `replace_an_snapshot` is the only full replace of that table.

Fresh `_migrate_0_to_1` may still create schema-1 tables; later migrates bring the file to **12**. New `_migrate_2_to_3` output plus `_migrate_3_to_4` plus `_migrate_4_to_5` plus `_migrate_5_to_6` plus `_migrate_6_to_7` plus `_migrate_7_to_8` plus `_migrate_8_to_9` plus `_migrate_9_to_10` plus `_migrate_10_to_11` plus `_migrate_11_to_12` is the supported shape. `annulled_transfer_names_json` / `annulled_sequences_json` on `kit_pipeline` are added by `_ensure_kit_pipeline_columns` on every `initialize` (do not bump schema for those columns alone).

Tables (names are normative):

### `google_kit`

One KSB ИД row per `(title, mark)` (case-insensitive identity). Columns D/E are **reference only**: `sheet_revision` / `sheet_appendix` / `sheet_revision_text`, `status_sheet`. `comment_raw` is column F unparsed.

### `google_event`

Parsed F lines for that kit: `kit_id`, `seq` (0-based order in the cell), `raw`, `event_date` (`DD.MM.YYYY` or NULL), `stage`, `stage_label`, `revision`, `appendix`, `transmittals_json` (JSON list of strings), `parsed`.

### `issuance_send`

**Every** parsed «Выдача РД ПД» row (not latest-wins). Same fields as `IssuanceKit`. Ingest uses `parse_issuance_sends` (all rows). `parse_issuance_matrix` remains latest-wins over the **raw** sheet for old tests. Комплекты «Выдача · …» paints `latest_effective_issuance_kits`.

### `kit_package`

One row per issued folder (or grey issuance-only stub):

- `source`: `rd` / `sq` / `robot` / `issuance_grey`
- `sequence`: folder `NN` or NULL
- `transfer_name`, `package_path` (folder, **never** the PDF path)
- `revision_text`: highest **filename** rev in that folder (OD wins ties), empty if unknown
- `max_mtime_ns`, `pdf_count`, `editable_count`
- `mto_revision_text`: filename rev of `mto_xlsx` in that folder, `''` if absent (delta overlay may keep MTO on an older NN)
- `overlay_current_count`: present files in this folder that are overlay-current
- `is_grey`: issuance send with this revision and **no** RD package
- `is_current`: latest **official** RD package for the kit (highest sequence among non-grey RD that are not working)
- `is_as_build`: 0/1 — any file in the package has canonical `is_as_build` (schema 4). Grey stubs are 0.

Robot rows: `package_path` = parent of the MTO file (`…\_ГОТОВЫЕ_ДЛЯ_РОБОТА\title\MARK`), `sequence` NULL.

### `kit_cycle`

One official send cycle: FK `send_id`, optional `package_id`, optional F event ids (`tdo_event_id`, `code_event_id`), `revision_text`, `match_reason` (`trm` | `revision` | `date`).

### `kit_pipeline`

PK `(title, mark)`: derived state for the **last official cycle of the official revision** (`_last_official_cycle`). Must **not** fall back to a send of another rev when overlay is working.

- `status` — **review only**: `not_uploaded` | `sent_tdo` | `tdo_review` | `agreed` (never `code_a`/`code_b`/`code_c`). Last official cycle of **official** rev.
- `code` — last letter `A`/`B`/`C` or NULL (F «согласовано» without a letter stores `A`). Same official cycle.
- `code_origin` — `customer`/`pi`/`unknown` or NULL; still about the last letter; tooltip only
- `code_stale` INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0
- `code_revision_text` TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT ''
- `code_date` TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT ''
- `tdo_date` TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '' — pass date of the last official cycle when `status` is `tdo_review` (F `tdo_passed`, else `incoming_passed`, else issuance incoming/send). Shown in `pipeline_review_label` as `Прошел ТДО (DD.MM.YYYY)` and in the tooltip (`pipeline_tdo_passed_date_text`). Empty column is filled on the next Google/`rebuild_pipeline`; the join layer can also take the date from F/issuance if the stored value is still empty. Added by initialize ALTER (do not bump schema for this column alone).
- `review_as_build` INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0
- `working_as_build` INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0 — as-build of a **working** folder whose filename rev is `working_revision_text` (Комплекты «Рабочая рев. РД» ` AB`). Not the kits as-build filter (`review_as_build` / official `row.rd.as_build`). Added by initialize ALTER (do not bump schema for this column alone).
- `working_revision_text` — working (informational / heatmap `W`); not kits current. May equal `official_revision_text` when another NN still has that filename rev.
- `working_transfer_names` / `working_sequences` — issued **folders** treated as working (manual flag and auto head). Комплекты / export / compare exclude **these folders**, not every package with the same filename rev and not every package that shares the same NN. `working_sequences` stores unique NN only; a duplicated `10_` is identified by folder name.
- `annulled_transfer_names` / `annulled_sequences` — issued **folders** marked «Аннулирована» (`kit_annulled_flag`). Same skip as working for official / export / compare, **plus** they lose the auto-working contest and drop out of transfer-order / closeness / heatmap collision join. Empty when none.
- `official_revision_text` — last issued rev that still exists on a non-working **and non-annulled** package; kits «РД · рев.», export, compare
- `suspicious`, `algorithm_version`

Historical `_migrate_2_to_3` CREATE of `kit_pipeline` stays as-is; v5 columns come from ALTER in `_migrate_4_to_5`. `tdo_date`, `working_as_build`, working-folder JSON, and annulled-folder JSON columns are added by `_ensure_kit_pipeline_columns` on every `initialize`.

### `kit_liquidity_review`

User decision, **not** truncated by scan/Google rebuild:

- Identity: `(title, mark, transfer_name, revision_text)` UNIQUE
- `sequence` nullable
- `decision`: `confirmed_ok` | `confirmed_illiquid`
- `comment` optional
- `evidence_mtime_ns`: package `max_mtime_ns` at decision time
- `decided_at` ISO UTC

If later files make `max_mtime_ns` **greater** than `evidence_mtime_ns` after `confirmed_ok`, derive pending suspicion again. `confirmed_illiquid` stays until the user changes it. Do not feed this table into overlay `detected_current`.

### `kit_working_flag`

Manual working-**folder** mark, **same survive-rebuild rule** as `kit_liquidity_review`. `_migrate_8_to_9` creates the table; `_migrate_9_to_10` rekeys identity to the issued folder. Never feed this table into overlay `detected_current`.

- Identity: `(title, mark, transfer_name)` UNIQUE NOCASE
- `revision_text` — filename rev of that folder (display / «Рабочая рев. РД»)
- `sequence` — folder `NN` (survives a rename of `10_рев.AN-01` → `10_рев.AN-03`)
- `decided_at` ISO UTC
- APIs: `upsert_working_flag` / `delete_working_flag` / `list_working_flags`

Working on disk (filename rev strictly higher than last effective send/F) does **not** need a row here. Unmark in «Все документы» deletes only this table. Two NN folders with the same filename revision can coexist: only the marked folder is working; the sibling stays official for Комплекты.

`upsert_working_flag` **deletes** `kit_annulled_flag` for the same `(title, mark, transfer_name)` (mutual exclusion). Overlay still ignores this table.

### `kit_annulled_flag`

Manual **annulled-folder** mark. Same survive-rebuild rule and same identity as `kit_working_flag`. `_migrate_11_to_12` creates the table. Never feed this table into overlay `detected_current`.

- Identity: `(title, mark, transfer_name)` UNIQUE NOCASE
- `revision_text` — filename rev of that folder (display)
- `sequence` — folder `NN`
- `decided_at` ISO UTC
- APIs: `upsert_annulled_flag` / `delete_annulled_flag` / `list_annulled_flags`
- **Only manual.** There is no auto-annulled. Unmark always deletes this row.

This is **not** `issuance_review.decision = "annulled"` (a send/orphan row in «Выдача · Журнал» that drops that send from the effective issuance contour). Folder-annulled hides one NN package; journal-annulled hides one issuance event.

`upsert_annulled_flag` **deletes** `kit_working_flag` for the same folder. Annulled wins if both rows somehow exist: the folder is not working.

Meaning: the package stays in «Все документы» (open/copy/rescan still work) but is **dead for contests**:

- not official («РД · рев.», export, RD↔robot, Auto MTO target, kits open-folder)
- not auto-working (even if it is overlay-current / newest NN)
- not «спорная» / closeness / сверка in «Проверить передачи»
- overlay `TRANSFER_*` / `DUP_SAME_REVISION` collisions that include a file from this folder are **dropped** when joining heatmap `problem_kinds` (scan overlay itself is unchanged)
- heatmap cell `annulled` / `Ан` when **all** RD packages of that filename rev are annulled; `list_mto_worklist` / `iter_mto_files_for_cells` skip that status like `working`

### `file_mtime_override`

User catalog date for one **MTO xlsx**. Same survive-rebuild rule as `kit_working_flag`. Scan still writes disk `file_entry.mtime_ns`. `list_files` substitutes `override_mtime_ns` into `FileRecord.data['mtime_ns']` only when the fingerprint still matches.

- Identity: `path_key` UNIQUE NOCASE
- Fingerprint: SHA-256 of `path_key|size|disk_mtime_ns` (scan identity). Unchanged file after rescan keeps the override. Size or disk mtime change → stale (disk date is used; row kept until the user resets)
- `override_date` TEXT `DD.MM.YYYY` (last F letter A, B, or C for that filename rev)
- `override_mtime_ns` local noon of that date (tree / «Проверить передачи» / history)
- `disk_mtime_ns` original scan mtime — tooltip / «на диске» only
- `reason` `code_a` | `code_b` | `code_c`
- APIs: `upsert_file_mtime_override` / `delete_file_mtime_override` / `get_file_mtime_override` / `list_file_mtime_overrides`
- GUI: Комплекты and history **«Заменить дату на дату последнего кода A/B/C»** / **«Сбросить дату каталога»**. Agreed-cycle scoring still uses last **code A** only. MTO compare cache uses `disk_mtime_ns` (`mto_file_stat_signature`)

### `issuance_review`

User issuance-journal decision, **same survive-rebuild rule** as `kit_liquidity_review`. `_migrate_6_to_7` creates the table. UNIQUE `(kind, identity_fingerprint)`. Never write decisions onto `issuance_send`.

| Field | Tokens / meaning |
|-------|------------------|
| `kind` | `send` \| `orphan` \| `manual` |
| `source` | `issuance` \| `google_f` \| `rd` \| `robot` \| `auto_mto` \| `manual` |
| `decision` | `''` \| `active` \| `legalized` \| `annulled` \| `erroneous` \| `duplicate` |
| `match_state` | `''` \| `matched` \| `unmatched` \| `ambiguous` |
| revision / send dates / TRMs / `sheet_status` / `note` / `comment` | copied from the sheet or typed |
| `identity_fingerprint` | SHA-256; **not** `issuance_send.id` / `row_index` |
| `evidence_fingerprint` | identity + sheet status + incoming + confirm TRM + note |
| `source_path` / `path_key` | display / robot·Auto MTO identity |
| `decided_at` | ISO UTC |

Identity (kind=`send`): SHA-256 of canon parts joined by `|`: `title`, `mark`, `revision_text`, `send_date_sortable`, `send_transmittal`. Evidence adds sheet status, incoming, confirm TRM, note.

`rematch_issuance_reviews` runs at the end of `ingest_google_snapshot` (after replace, before GUI `rebuild_pipeline`). Ladder: exact identity; else unique (rev+date); else unique (rev+TRM) if both TRMs set; 0 → `unmatched`; >1 → `ambiguous`. Decision/comment kept.

Effective contour — [`effective_issuance_sends`](rd_catalog/issuance_review.py) / [`latest_effective_issuance_kits`](rd_catalog/issuance_review.py): INCLUDE `active`, `legalized`; EXCLUDE `annulled`, `erroneous`, `duplicate`, empty. Sheet send with no review = implicit `active`. Legalized orphan/manual: `send_id` None, `match_reason=legalized`, empty date loses latest-wins. Legalize requires `revision_text`. Exclude statuses require comment (`validate_issuance_decision`). Other issuance columns are optional.

Consumers of effective sends: `rebuild_pipeline`, grey packages, `rebuild_revision_matrix`, `list_mto_worklist` (`in_issuance`), `get_kit_card` issuance latest, startup hydrate, kits `_rebuild_kit_rows`. Raw snapshot stays complete. `REV_MISMATCH` uses the issuance object passed into `build_kit_matrix` (effective latest). Auto MTO content compare / overlay / ban / MTO pins unchanged. Heatmap GUI still requires canonical RD files for a kit **row**; legalize adds a **cell** when RD exists.

### `an_mto_file`

Dump index only. Not overlay. Not `SourceKind` (no `SourceKind.AN`). Not `file_entry`.

Columns: `path` UNIQUE, `path_key`, `title`, `mark`, `revision_text`, `core_stem`, `discipline_block`, `name`, `parent_dir`, `mtime_ns`, `size`, `scanned_at`.

Index `(title COLLATE NOCASE, mark COLLATE NOCASE)`.

`replace_an_snapshot` deletes+inserts that table only; does not touch `file_entry` / overlay / `issuance_review` / `kit_liquidity_review` / `kit_working_flag` / `kit_annulled_flag`.

Cancelled walk / disabled `an_root` must not call replace.

Read APIs: `list_an_mto_files`, `list_an_files_by_kit`.

### `kit_revision_cell` (schema 4)

Derived heatmap snapshot. PK `(title, mark, revision_text)` case-insensitive. Replaced by `rebuild_revision_matrix` (full catalog, or only `kit_keys` after a folder-scoped rescan). Does not delete `kit_liquidity_review`, `issuance_review`, `an_mto_file`, `kit_working_flag`, or `kit_annulled_flag`.

| Column | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| `revision_text` | Filename revision (`01`, `01-AN02`, `0`, `V`/`S`) |
| `pipeline_status` | Fill key: `no_mto` / `not_uploaded` / `sent_tdo` / `tdo_review` / `code_a` / `code_b` / `code_c` / `working` / `annulled`. Do **not** persist `empty` — missing row = empty GUI cell. |
| `letters` | Display tokens joined with `·`, e.g. `A·AB`, `T`, `W`, `–`, `AB` |
| `is_as_build` | File/path as-build **or** F `us_build` on this revision |
| `is_current` | Official-current RD MTO exists at this filename rev (when overlay is working, this is the official rev, not `W`) |
| `is_current_ifc` | This rev is the highest filename rev among **present RD files with `is_as_build=0`** (OD wins ties). Independent of overlay. |
| `has_mto` | Present RD `mto_xlsx` with this filename rev |
| `problem_kinds_json` | JSON list of collision kinds and/or `liquidity` |
| `package_ids_json` | JSON list of `kit_package.id` for this kit+rev (RD first) |
| `algorithm_version` | `REVISION_MATRIX_ALGORITHM_VERSION` |

One cell per `(title, mark, filename rev)`. Several NN folders with the same filename rev share the cell (tooltip lists packages).

## 2b. Canonical as-build (`is_as_build`)

Helper `path_is_as_build(path: str) -> bool` in `rd_catalog/parse.py` (lexical, UNC-safe, no disk IO): any **directory** segment (not the filename) matches existing `_AS_BUILD_RE`. Transfer-folder parse still sets `TransferMetadata.is_as_build` from the NN name.

On persist, `file_entry.transfer_is_as_build` stores the **canonical OR**: transfer-folder flag **or** `path_is_as_build(path)`. Column name is historical; readers treat it as file-level `is_as_build`. Do not add a second `file_entry` column.

`kit_package.is_as_build` = any file in that package group has canonical as-build.

Overlay **must not** drop as-build files. Dual current: overlay `detected_current` (objective newest, may be working) vs `is_current_ifc` (max IFC filename rev). Kits / export / compare use official ids, not the working head.

## 3. F-stage classifier (`kits.py`)

Keep `_STAGE_PATTERNS` as the only classifier. Add (order matters: `code_c` **before** `code_b` so «код C/С» is not eaten):

| `stage` | Label | Intent |
|---------|--------|--------|
| `code_c` | код C | Latin C or Cyrillic С after `код` |
| `sr_upload` | загрузка в СР | «загрузк…СР», «отпр…на загрузку» |
| `us_build` | US-BUILD | `us-build` / `us build` / `as-build` / `as-built` in F text; **journal + matrix `AB` only** |
| existing | код А, код B, ТДО, входной контроль, ДУП, корректировка, согласовано | unchanged |

`code_b` pattern must not match C/С. Place `us_build` **before** the implicit `other` fallback (after `agreed` is fine). `us_build` must **not** be in `_CODE_STAGES` / `_PASSED_STAGES` / `_SENT_STAGES` and must **not** drive `KitPipelineStatus`. «корр. в раб. пор», NanoCAD, «выпустить до» stay `other`.

Column F is the event source of truth. D/E stay stored and shown as secondary.

## 4. Package path

`issued_package_dir(path: str) -> str` in `rd_catalog/parse.py` (lexical, no disk IO):

1. Split UNC-safe segments (keep `\\server\share`).
2. Drop the filename.
3. Drop a trailing media segment: `PDF` / `DWG` / `BBB` / `ПДФ` (any case).
4. If the last remaining segment is an issued transfer (`is_transfer_folder_name` with `under_gate` from ancestors), return that folder path.
5. Else return the parent after step 3 (robot / SQ / mark folder).

Example file → package:

`\\bcc\eng\...\РД\9110\06_KSB_21\Для передачи\05_рев.0-AN02_AGCC.287-9110-KSB1\PDF\AGCC.287-9110-KSB1.OD-0001_0-AN02_RU.pdf`

→ `\\bcc\eng\...\РД\9110\06_KSB_21\Для передачи\05_рев.0-AN02_AGCC.287-9110-KSB1`

NN is the **folder sequence**, not the document revision. One filename revision may occupy several NN folders (PI B/C resent without bumping AN).

## 5. Pipeline status (current kit)

Two independent fields on the **last official cycle of `official_revision_text`** (last send of that rev; if no RD, latest **effective** issuance rev of that official rev). `_last_official_cycle` must **not** fall back to a send of another rev when overlay is working.

Kit-level cell strings are `pipeline_review_label` / `pipeline_approval_label`. Display version is `PIPELINE_DISPLAY_VERSION` in [`rd_catalog/pipeline.py`](rd_catalog/pipeline.py) (v2 active; flip to `PIPELINE_DISPLAY_V1` to restore previous labels). `_review_status` / `code_stale` are unchanged. `РД` is the official package in the RD folder (same as column «РД · рев.»), not working and not Google D/E. Folder-tree `review_full` stays `pipeline_status_label` only (no РД, no dates, no B/C). Full cell/Подсказки contract: [AI_rd_catalog_pipeline_status.mdc](.cursor/rules/AI_rd_catalog_pipeline_status.mdc).

### Статус рассмотрения (`kit_pipeline.status`)

Progress of the **last** cycle. B/C never go here.

| Value | Label |
|-------|--------|
| `not_uploaded` | Не загружен в СР |
| `sent_tdo` | Отправлен на ТДО |
| `tdo_review` | Прошел ТДО |
| `agreed` | Согласован |

Meaning:

- no issuance and no F `sr_upload` / `tdo_sent` / `incoming_sent` for this official revision → `not_uploaded`
- uploaded, incoming/TDO not passed → `sent_tdo`
- incoming/TDO passed on **this cycle**, and this cycle has neither code A nor F `agreed` → `tdo_review` (**even if an actual B/C hangs on the kit**)
- this cycle has code A **or** F `agreed` → `agreed`

F «согласовано» without letter A: review `agreed`; stored `code` is `A` (v2 approval shows `—`; the letter is the review status).

If the official-cycle package `is_as_build`: append ` (AB)` to the review **text**. Color unchanged. As-build is an ordinary later issuance, not a special status. After a new as-build cycle, a previous A is **stale** (grey), not green “IFC still alive”. Issued as-build that **matches** last send stays official with `(AB)` (5500-style), not working.

### Статус согласования (`kit_pipeline.code`)

Last kit letter in F order (`A`/`B`/`C`), else `—` with no fill.

Code is **current** if it belongs to the current review cycle:

- strong: send TRM equals a transmittal on the code event
- else same filename rev **and** the last official cycle did **not** start after the code (no later send/TDO of this official rev with a different TRM / later date than the code)
- do **not** treat a code as current only because filename rev matches when the send TRM differs and the code date is earlier than this cycle’s send/TDO (9000-KSB)

Code is **stale** (`code_stale=1`) when a letter exists but it is not this cycle: other TRM, lower rev, or same rev with a later TDO/send (9000-KSB). Cell strings and tooltip outline: [AI_rd_catalog_pipeline_status.mdc](.cursor/rules/AI_rd_catalog_pipeline_status.mdc) (`pipeline_review_tooltip` / `pipeline_approval_tooltip` in [`rd_catalog/monitor_views.py`](rd_catalog/monitor_views.py)). v2 shows the letter in approval only when stale (`pipeline_approval_shows_letter`); current B/C sit on review after the pass date; current A is not duplicated.

**Colors (cells only, never the whole row):**

- review: existing `not_uploaded` / `sent_tdo` / `tdo_review`; `agreed` uses `#137333` (F-palette key `agreed`)
- v1 current approval: `code_a` green, `code_b` orange, `code_c` red
- stale approval: palette key `approval_stale` (~`#80868b`)
- empty approval (including v2 this-cycle letters): unpainted

Expected 9000-KSB: review **Прошел ТДО (… ) · РД …** (no B), approval grey `B · … · 20.08.2026 · прошлый цикл`.
Expected 7700-POS current B (v2): review **Прошел ТДО (10.06.2026) · B · РД 01 · отпр. 01.06.2026**, approval `—`.

**Heatmap keeps `working` / `W` and `annulled` / `Ан`:** `kit_revision_cell.pipeline_status` still uses per-filename-rev `_last_code_on_revision` then TDO/sent (`code_a|b|c` / `tdo_review` / …), then working — **except** a fully-annulled filename rev is `annulled` first (no F letter on that cell). A cell on rev `0` may still show letter B when a non-annulled package remains. Do not recolor READY/WARNING. Documents-tree badge is the folder **review** status (not the approval letter; `review_full` has no kit-level rev). Kit-level review labels include official rev via `pipeline_review_label`.

### Codes A/B/C origin

- **A** → always `customer` (Заказчик).
- **B/C** → if a **later official** send or later RD package has a **higher** filename revision → `customer`; if the next official send keeps the **same** revision → `pi`. Otherwise `unknown`.
- Approval letter display is versioned (`pipeline_approval_shows_letter`); origin is tooltip only.

### Working revision (not an error)

**Рабочая ревизия** = overlay-current filename rev **strictly higher** than last effective send/F, **or** a user-marked **issued folder** in «Все документы» (`kit_working_flag`). Expected (local work before the next issuance). Leftover files in an **earlier** NN whose filename ranks higher (`01` vs later `0-AN01`) are not auto-working. **Annulled folders are not candidates** (`kit_annulled_flag`): overlay-current among remaining non-annulled packages is the auto-working head. The working mark excludes that NN from Комплекты official / export / compare; a sibling folder with the same filename rev stays official. Column **«Рабочая рев. РД»** shows the working folder’s filename rev **only when it strictly outranks** official «РД · рев.» (`working_revision_for_display` / `format_working_rd_rev_label`); equal or lower → «—». Appends ` AB` when `working_as_build` (working folder as-build).

It is **not** liquidity and must not be painted as a pipeline error. It is also **not** kits current («РД · рев.» / review-approval of that rev use **official**), **not** robot export / spec pick, **not** RD↔robot MTO compare, **not** Auto MTO target (unless pin / heatmap export selection), **not** «MTO · Перечень» rows. GUI column **«Рабочая рев. РД»** is informational (issuance lag). Overlay `detected_current` stays objective newest. Helpers: `official_detected_current_ids`, `official_rd_mto_overlay`. Unmark only **manual** flags; auto (disk > last send) cannot be unmarked.

When overlay is working: official = last issued rev that still exists on a non-working **and non-annulled** package (may be the same filename rev as the working folder). Do not grey a code merely because `working_revision_text` is higher. `REV_MISMATCH` vs Google D remains a highlight of sheet vs **official** RD (kits matrix uses official ids). The issuance object passed into `build_kit_matrix` is the **effective** latest (`latest_effective_issuance_kits`), not a raw snapshot row.

Example 2000-KSB: review **Согласован · РД 01-AN01**, approval **—** (v2 current A), «РД · рев.» **01-AN01**, «Рабочая рев. РД» **01-AN02 AB**, heatmap 01-AN02 still `W·AB`.

### Annulled folder (not a journal decision)

**Аннулирована** = user-marked issued NN folder (`kit_annulled_flag`). Only from «Все документы» revision-node context **«Пометить папку как аннулированную»**. There is no auto-annulled.

**Not** `issuance_review.decision=annulled` (журнал выдачи). Journal-annulled drops a **send**. Folder-annulled drops a **package** from contests while files stay in the tree.

| Contest / consumer | Working folder | Annulled folder |
|---|---|---|
| Overlay `detected_current` | unchanged (may still be «Текущая») | unchanged (may still be «Текущая») |
| Official / «РД · рев.» / export / RD↔robot / Auto MTO target / kits open-folder | skip this NN | skip this NN |
| Auto-working contest (newest NN > last send/F) | this folder **can win** | this folder **cannot win**; next non-annulled overlay-current competes |
| Heatmap fill | `working` / `W` when **all** packages of that filename rev are working | `annulled` / `Ан` when **all** packages of that filename rev are annulled (wins over F codes on that rev) |
| `list_mto_worklist` / `iter_mto_files_for_cells` | skip `working` | skip `annulled` |
| «Проверить передачи» inversion / closeness / сверка | shown as роль «рабочая»; not «спорная»; not current | shown as роль «аннулирована»; not «спорная»; not current; not closeness winner |
| Heatmap `problem_kinds` from overlay `TRANSFER_*` / `DUP_SAME_REVISION` | still joined (working does **not** hide overlay collisions) | **drop** the collision when any `path_key` sits in an annulled folder |
| Kit card package row | роль «рабочая» | роль «аннулирована» |
| Tree word / fill | always «рабочая», palette `working` | always «аннулирована», palette `annulled` |
| Unmark | manual flag only; auto remains | always (flag is only manual) |

Mutual exclusion: marking working deletes the annulled row for that folder and vice versa. Annulled wins if both exist. Sibling NN of the same filename rev stays in play.

3860-SOT example: leftover `08_рев.01_…` marked working still keeps overlay `transfer_order_conflict` on the heatmap cell. Annul that NN → official/working contests ignore it, heatmap problems from that folder vanish, later `0-AN01` can be official without competing against `01`.

### Liquidity suspicion (late edits of the **same** issued revision)

Anchor date for a revision: F `tdo_passed` date, else issuance `incoming_control_date`, else send date.

Look at RD `kit_package` rows whose `revision_text` equals that official revision. If `max_mtime_ns` local **calendar month** is **strictly after** the anchor’s calendar month → pending suspicious (example: TDO 01.09, September mtimes OK, December mtime not). Same-month working-order edits are OK.

Do **not** flag «revision on disk higher than last send» as suspicious.

Paint the package row. User actions: confirm OK / confirm illiquid. Persist in `kit_liquidity_review`. Overlay unchanged.

Grey issuance-only rows (`is_grey`) are not liquidity-checked (no folder).

## 6. Matching sends to F to packages (`match_*`)

For each `issuance_send`, find F events and an RD package:

1. **TRM** — `send_transmittal` equals an event transmittal (strongest).
2. Else **revision** — `revision_text` equals event/package filename rev.
3. Else **date** — event date within ±2 days of send or incoming-control date.

Unmatched F events still appear in the card journal for that kit. Unmatched issuance with no RD package → grey `kit_package`.

`kit_cycle.code_event_id` must **not** attach a revision-only A/B/C when the send TRM differs and the code date is earlier than this cycle’s send/TDO (9000-KSB). Heatmap still sees that letter on the filename rev via `_last_code_on_revision`.

## 7. Read API (Qt-free)

`rd_catalog/pipeline.py`:

- `rebuild_pipeline(database: CatalogDatabase, *, records, detected_current_ids, kit_keys=None) -> None`  
  Rebuilds `kit_package`, `kit_cycle`, `kit_pipeline`, then `kit_revision_cell`. Uses `effective_issuance_sends` (grey packages and cycles follow the include contour). Does not delete `kit_liquidity_review`, `issuance_review`, `an_mto_file`, `kit_working_flag`, `kit_annulled_flag`, or `file_mtime_override`. F events load once via `list_google_events_by_kit` (no per-kit SQL). `kit_keys` set → delete+insert only those identities; other kits stay. Empty `kit_keys` = full rebuild.
- `official_detected_current_ids(records, detected_current_ids, pipelines) -> set[int]`  
  Overlay-current ids with working **and annulled** kits removed. Promotion is the issued **package** whose highest filename rev is `official_revision_text`; if that exact filename is missing (send/F ``01-AN01``, disk still ``01``), the newest **non-working and non-annulled** package is used so open-folder and disk «РД · рев.» stay on that NN. The kits cell then appends ``01-AN01 Нет в РД`` (grey). Working/annulled packages are skipped by **folder name** (`working_transfer_names` / `annulled_transfer_names`); `*_sequences` is a unique-NN fallback only. Two folders with the same NN (``10_SQ-…`` IFC and ``10_рев.…_as built``) are different packages — the as-build must not hide the IFC sibling. Leftover files in the working folder that still carry the official name do not win. Never feeds `kit_working_flag` / `kit_annulled_flag` into overlay `detected_current`. Kits with **only** annulled folders (no working head) still go through this promotion so overlay-current on an annulled newest NN is not official.
- `records_in_contour(records, rd_root, *, previous_records=None, previous_contour=None) -> Sequence[FileRecord]`  
  SQ/ROBOT plus RD on a canonical issued path. GUI `refresh` runs this once and then passes `rd_root=None` into pipeline / worklist / kit matrix. Optional previous snapshot reuses membership when `id`/path/source did not change.
- `official_rd_mto_overlay(database, *, records=None) -> OverlayResult`  
  RD MTO overlay for robot compare: working **and annulled** packages out; official-package MTO in when overlay was working or the newest NN is annulled. Pass already-loaded `records` from the GUI so enqueue after scan does not `list_files` again.
- `pipeline_algorithm_needs_rebuild(pipelines) -> bool`  
  True when any stored `kit_pipeline.algorithm_version` is older than `PIPELINE_STATUS_ALGORITHM_VERSION`. Empty list is False (the empty-derived hatch covers that). Startup hydrate and `CatalogWindow._should_rebuild_empty_derived` use it so v3 rows are not painted as official overlay.
- `kit_keys_under_folders(records, folders) -> set[tuple[str, str]]`  
  Identities whose `file_entry.path` sits under a scoped rescan prefix (including `present=0`).
- `rebuild_revision_matrix(database, *, records, detected_current_ids, kit_keys=None) -> None`  
  Called from `rebuild_pipeline` after `replace_kit_derived` so `package_ids_json` uses real SQLite ids. Joins collisions via `path_keys` → `file_entry` → title/mark/filename-rev. Same `kit_keys` contract. Issuance side is `effective_issuance_sends` (legalize can add a **cell** when RD exists; heatmap GUI still needs canonical RD files for a kit **row**).
- `get_kit_card(database, title, mark) -> KitCard | None`  
  Issuance latest is the last effective send for that kit, not a raw `issuance_send` row.
- `list_kit_pipelines(database) -> tuple[KitPipelineRow, ...]` for the комплекты table (**«Статус рассмотрения»** via `pipeline_review_label` + **«Статус согласования»** columns).
- `list_folder_tree_hints(database) -> dict[tuple[str, str, str], FolderTreeHint]` for «Все документы» revision labels. Key is `(title.casefold(), mark.casefold(), transfer_or_folder.casefold())`. `review_status` is empty when no cycle matched that folder. `review_full` stays without kit-level rev (`pipeline_status_label`, not `pipeline_review_label`). As-build on the tree is `folder_has_as_build` from `file_entry` / scan records (canonical path+transfer flag), not F parse. `is_working` / `working_origin` as today. `is_annulled` is true when the package folder is in `kit_pipeline.annulled_transfer_names` (manual flag). MTO fields (`mto_status`, `mto_letters`, `mto_revision_text`, `has_mto_file`, `is_current_mto`, `is_current_ifc`, `problem_kinds`) come from the `kit_revision_cell` snapshot. Cell resolved by `_package_mto_revision`: `package.mto_revision_text` when non-empty, else `package.revision_text` (a delta can carry PDFs on rev `02` and the MTO on rev `01`). `has_mto_file` = an MTO xlsx physically in that package folder; it is **not** `kit_revision_cell.has_mto` (kit+revision scope). `mto_status` is empty when no cell matched. Cells are loaded once per `list_folder_tree_hints` call, not per package.
- `list_revision_matrix(database) -> tuple[KitRevisionRow, ...]` grouped/sorted for the heatmap. GUI may also call `list_revision_columns(cells)` as the union of `revision_text` sorted by `revision_rank`.
- `iter_mto_files_for_cells(database, *, records, predicate) -> tuple[FileRecord, ...]`  
  Present RD `mto_xlsx` whose `(title, mark, revision_text)` matches selected cells. **Excludes** `pipeline_status == "working"` and `pipeline_status == "annulled"`. Predicates: `code_a`, `tdo_passed` (`tdo_review` or any `code_*` on **kit_revision_cell**), `current` (`is_current` — official when overlay is working), `current_ifc` (`is_current_ifc`), `exclude_as_build`. Unknown predicate → `ValueError`. Resolves paths from `records` / `file_entry`, never from table text. Overlay flags come from the last `rebuild_revision_matrix` snapshot (`detected_current_ids` is not a query argument). Shares private index `_mto_records_by_kit_revision` (present RD `mto_xlsx` by kit identity and filename revision) with `list_mto_worklist`. Keeps `revision_texts_equivalent` matching because `_revision_dedupe_key` is not equivalent for letter revisions (`V`/`S`). No UNC copy.
- `list_mto_worklist(database, *, records) -> tuple[MtoWorklistRow, ...]`  
  One row per `kit_revision_cell`, in `list_revision_matrix` order, **except** `pipeline_status == "working"` and `pipeline_status == "annulled"` skipped **after** recording `cell_keys` (kit is not synthesized as `no_rd`). Frozen dataclass: `title`, `mark`, `revision_text`, `status`, `letters`, `is_as_build`, `is_current`, `is_current_ifc`, `has_mto`, `mto_path`, `mto_mtime_ns`, `package_path`, `package_label`, `package_count`, `problem_kinds`, `gap_kind`. `gap_kind`: `no_package` when no non-grey RD package is linked, else `no_mto_file` when no present RD `mto_xlsx` matched, else empty. `in_issuance` is true when an **effective** send exists for that kit+rev. Paths from `records` / `file_entry`, never GUI text. Exported from `rd_catalog/__init__.py` with `MtoWorklistRow`. Read view over `kit_revision_cell` — **no extra schema bump**.
- [`rd_catalog/issuance_review.py`](rd_catalog/issuance_review.py) (Qt-free): `rematch_issuance_reviews`, `effective_issuance_sends`, `latest_effective_issuance_kits`, `list_issuance_journal`, `apply_journal_decision`, `validate_issuance_decision`. Persist via `CatalogDatabase.upsert_issuance_review` / `list_issuance_reviews` / `get_issuance_review`.

### Per-revision pipeline (heatmap fill)

Reuse `_last_code_on_revision` then `_review_status` **scoped to that filename revision** (cycles + F events + issuance sends on that rev), not `kit_pipeline` (current kit only). Kit-level `agreed` is not a heatmap fill key unless there is a real `code_a` event.

Priority:

1. **All** RD packages of this filename rev are annulled → `annulled`; letter `Ан` (do not paint F codes on a fully-annulled rev)
2. F code on this rev → `code_a` / `code_b` / `code_c`; letter `A`/`B`/`C`
3. Else TDO/incoming passed or accepted issuance on this rev → `tdo_review`; letter `T`
4. Else sent/sr_upload on this rev → `sent_tdo`
5. Else this rev is strictly higher than last official (`working_revision_text`) and present on disk → `working`; letter `W`
6. Else present RD MTO at this rev → `not_uploaded`
7. Else RD PDF/package at this rev but no MTO → `no_mto`; letter `–`
8. Else do not insert a row (GUI `empty`)

Always append `AB` to `letters` when canonical as-build or F `us_build` on this rev. Problem kinds: `transfer_order_conflict`, `transfer_mtime_conflict`, `dup_same_revision`, `file_missing`, plus `liquidity` when a package of this rev is pending-suspicious. Overlay collisions whose **any** `path_key` is in an annulled folder are omitted from this join.

When computing heatmap `is_current` / `is_current_ifc`, skip files that sit in annulled folders (overlay-current on an annulled newest NN must not underline that cell).

`KitCard` (frozen dataclass): identity, matrix summary **not** recomputed here (window still uses `build_kit_matrix` for Совпадает / gaps; issuance argument is effective latest), `pipeline`, `working_revision_text`, sources snapshot paths as **package** dirs, `packages: tuple[KitPackageRow, ...]` including `is_as_build`, cycles grouped per package (multiline Выдача / F), Google D/E reference fields, issuance latest (effective contour, for the old columns).

MTO on the card = `mto_revision_text` per package. Do **not** show READY/WARNING on the kit card.

## 8. Ingest

`GoogleKitsLoadResult.issuance_sends` is **every** parsed Выдача row (`parse_issuance_sends`). `issuance_kits` on the load result remains latest-wins over the **raw** sheet for old tests/columns. After ingest the GUI paints `latest_effective_issuance_kits`.

After `fetch_google_kits` / cache hydrate, `ingest_google_snapshot` → `CatalogDatabase.replace_google_snapshot` replaces `google_kit` + `google_event` + `issuance_send` in one transaction (does **not** delete `issuance_review`, `an_mto_file`, `kit_working_flag`, or `kit_annulled_flag`), then `rematch_issuance_reviews`. `CatalogWindow.refresh` then `rebuild_pipeline` (packages + revision matrix) when `rebuild_derived` is true. File scans and Google-**load**-thread completion pass `ingest_google=False` so the snapshot is not rewritten a second time. F-write completion ingests in `_apply_google_write_snapshot` (already fetched) and must **not** call `refresh()`; it scopes `rebuild_pipeline` with `changed_google_kit_keys` plus successful write jobs. Normal process start passes `rebuild_derived=False`. Palette: `rd_catalog/status_colors.py` + dialog; JSON `runtime_dir/status_colors.json`. Extra heatmap keys: `empty`, `no_mto`, `working`, `annulled`, `problem`, `current`, `us_build` (defaults in `default_palette()`).

Call `rebuild_pipeline` from GUI `refresh()` after a scan or Google load so packages follow the last walk (`rebuild_derived` defaults True). Folder-scoped rescan (`rd_subtree` / `sq_subtree` / `robot_subtree`) passes those prefixes as `pipeline_subtrees`; derived rows rebuild only for `kit_keys_under_folders`. Full catalog scan still rebuilds every kit. Overlay in `store_scan` stays global (all present RD files) — do not invent a partial overlay. After missing detection a reliable RD `store_scan` clears `schema_meta.noncanonical_rd_clean` (does not walk all RD paths). Startup hydrate runs `purge_noncanonical_rd_files(..., skip_if_clean=True)` before `list_files`: skip when the flag is `1`, otherwise delete non-canonical RD rows and set the flag. Canonical `present=0` stays. Robot-only and unreliable RD scans do not purge and do not clear the flag. Qt «Все документы» tree full-rebuilds on a full scan and on a documents-tab folder rescan (`stay_on_documents`); keep_view (Пересканировать РД / робот MTO / SQ→RD) defers it.

`parse_issuance_sends(rows)` returns all `IssuanceKit` rows; keep `parse_issuance_matrix` as latest-wins for existing tests/matrix.

## 9. GUI monitor (`window.py`)

- Bottom splitter: `QTabWidget` — **Карточка** (default) + **Текст** (current `QPlainTextEdit` dump). No «Файлы» tab; files stay in «Все документы».
- Card fills from `get_kit_card` only. Two badges: `pipeline_review_label` (includes official rev) + `pipeline_approval_label` (`A · rev · date`, or `—`). Header also shows an MTO rollup from `list_mto_worklist` (`MTO: тек. рев. … · <short status> · нет файла: N · проблемы: N`; `MTO: нет данных` when none). Buttons «Папка РД» / four package actions (открыть папку / копировать путь / показать в «Все документы» / «Передать роботу») share context-menu handlers; enabled from `_update_action_states`. Double-click opens **package** path (`issued_package_dir` of `paths[0]` or `kit_package.package_path`). Copy paths copies package dirs. Color legend next to the buttons; repaints on `_reload_status_colors`.
